any portion of Paprika source code, you must provide visible attribution in
the product's user interface.

The attribution must:

a. include the project name "Paprika";

b. include the text "By Batsun";

c. be reasonably visible and readable to an ordinary user;

d. appear in a user-accessible location such as the main menu, settings
   screen, credits screen, about screen, information screen, or another
   comparable interface; and

e. not be hidden, removed, obscured, made intentionally difficult to find,
   or presented in a misleading way.

Examples of acceptable attribution include:

    Paprika — By Batsun

or:

    Contains code from Paprika — By Batsun

If the work has no user interface, the attribution requirement must instead
be satisfied by prominently including both "Paprika" and "By Batsun" in the
project's README, documentation, package metadata, or another place normally
seen by recipients of the work.

